body:
![medium](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/medium-priority.svg)

In the print media query, the background and color are set using hardcoded values and `!important`. Since the variables are already redefined for the print context in the `:root` block (lines 574-582), it is better to use those variables and avoid `!important` to maintain a cleaner cascade.

```suggestion
    background: var(--report-paper);
    color: var(--report-ink);
```

