![medium](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/medium-priority.svg)

The Mermaid node extraction logic currently only handles a single arrow per line because it uses `split("-->", 1)`. Mermaid flowcharts frequently use chained arrows (e.g., `A --> B --> C`). Refactoring this to split on all occurrences and iterate through the resulting parts would support these common linear diagram patterns.

```suggestion
        parts = [p.strip() for p in line.split("-->")]
        for i in range(len(parts) - 1):
            for node in (parts[i], parts[i+1]):
                label = re.sub(r"^[A-Za-z0-9_]+\[([^\]]+)\]$", r"\1", node).strip()
                if label and label not in nodes:
                    nodes.append(label)
```

