![medium](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/medium-priority.svg)

Several of the added `jq` projection expressions contain redundant operations and overly complex nesting. Simplifying these expressions improves readability and maintainability:

1. `((.merged_at // null) != null or (.merged // false) == true)` can be simplified to `(.merged_at != null or .merged == true)` because `null` and `false` are already the default falsy values for these checks.
2. `((.state // "") | ascii_upcase)` can be simplified to `(.state // "" | ascii_upcase)` by removing redundant outer parentheses.
3. `(.merged_by // null)` is equivalent to `.merged_by` since a missing or null key in `jq` already evaluates to `null`.

```suggestion
		state) projection="${projection}${projection:+,}state: (if (.merged_at != null or .merged == true) then \"MERGED\" else (.state // \"\" | ascii_upcase) end)" ;;
		merged) projection="${projection}${projection:+,}merged: (.merged == true or .merged_at != null)" ;;
		mergedAt) projection="${projection}${projection:+,}mergedAt: .merged_at" ;;
		closedAt) projection="${projection}${projection:+,}closedAt: .closed_at" ;;
		mergeCommit) projection="${projection}${projection:+,}mergeCommit: (if (.merge_commit_sha // \"\") != \"\" then {oid: .merge_commit_sha} else null end)" ;;
		mergedBy) projection="${projection}${projection:+,}mergedBy: .merged_by" ;;
```

