![high](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/high-priority.svg)

### Bug Analysis & Improvement Opportunity

There are three critical issues with the current implementation of `_hasPriorSameCommandBodyFileCreation`:

1. **Naive `ghWrite` Regex Search**: Using `cmd.search(...)` with the `ghWrite` regex finds the *first* `gh` command in the entire string. If a command chain contains multiple `gh` commands (e.g., `gh issue create ... && echo "body" > foo.md && gh issue comment 1 --body-file foo.md`), `ghWrite` will be `0` (the index of the first `gh` command), causing the function to return `false` immediately and fail to detect the creation of `foo.md` for the second command.
2. **False Positives in Quotes/Heredocs**: If there is a false-positive `gh` pattern inside a quoted string or heredoc earlier in the command chain (e.g., `memory-helper.sh store --content "gh issue create fails" && echo "body" > foo.md && gh issue comment 1 --body-file foo.md`), `cmd.search` will match the false positive, slicing the command too early and failing to detect the file creation.
3. **Missing `echo` Support**: `echo` is one of the most common ways to write content to a file in shell scripts (e.g., `echo "body" > foo.md`). Excluding it from the `creationPatterns` list will cause valid `echo`-based file creation chains to be blocked.

### Solution

Since `_repairBodyFile` is only called when `--body-file` is present, we can target the exact argument we want to repair by using `cmd.lastIndexOf("--body-file")` as the boundary. This is extremely robust, completely avoids false positives, handles multiple `gh` commands correctly, and simplifies the logic. We also add `echo` to the list of allowed creation commands.

```javascript
function _hasPriorSameCommandBodyFileCreation(cmd, filePath) {
  if (!filePath) return false;
  const bodyFileIdx = cmd.lastIndexOf("--body-file");
  if (bodyFileIdx === -1) return false;
  const beforeGh = cmd.slice(0, bodyFileIdx);
  if (!beforeGh.includes(filePath)) return false;
  const escaped = filePath.replace(/[.*+?^${}()|[\]\\]/g, "\\$&");
  const quotedPath = `["']?${escaped}["']?`;
  const creationPatterns = [
    new RegExp(`(?:^|[;&|]|&&|\\|\\|)\\s*(?:printf|cat|tee|echo)\\b[\\s\\S]*(?:>|>>)\\s*${quotedPath}`),
    new RegExp(`(?:^|[;&|]|&&|\\|\\|)\\s*(?:cp|mv)\\b[\\s\\S]+\\s+${quotedPath}`),
    new RegExp(`(?:^|[;&|]|&&|\\|\\|)\\s*touch\\s+${quotedPath}`),
  ];
  return creationPatterns.some((pattern) => pattern.test(beforeGh));
}
```

