body:
![medium](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/medium-priority.svg)

Using `cmd.lastIndexOf("--body-file")` is imprecise and can fail or return the wrong index if there are multiple `--body-file` arguments in the command, or if the string appears in unrelated contexts (e.g., comments or echo statements). It is much safer and more precise to locate the exact `--body-file` argument that corresponds to the target `filePath`.

```javascript
  const escaped = filePath.replace(/[.*+?^${}()|[\]\\]/g, "\\$&amp;");
  const bodyFilePattern = new RegExp("\\\\b--body-file(?:\\\\s+|=)[\"']?" + escaped + "[\"']?");
  const match = cmd.match(bodyFilePattern);
  if (!match || match.index <= 0) return false;
  const beforeGh = cmd.slice(0, match.index);
  if (!beforeGh.includes(filePath)) return false;
  const quotedPath = "[\"']?" + escaped + "[\"']?";
```

