![medium](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/medium-priority.svg)

The current implementation constructs the `long_csv` string using a loop with `seq`, which is slow in Bash due to repeated string reallocations and relies on an external command. Additionally, the subshell assignment to `early_close_output` is redundant and can be simplified by directly redirecting the pipeline output to the log file.

We can optimize this by using Bash brace expansion and `tr` to generate the CSV string instantly, and by simplifying the pipeline redirection.

```suggestion
long_csv=$(echo token-{1..7000} | tr ' ' ',')

early_close_stderr=$({
	_rest_split_csv "$long_csv" | {
		IFS= read -r first_token || true
		printf '%s\n' "$first_token"
	} >"$TMP/early-close-output.log"
} 2>&1)
```

