body:
![medium](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/medium-priority.svg)

Calling `statSync(path)` directly after `existsSync(path)` introduces a potential TOCTOU (time-of-check to time-of-use) race condition if the path is deleted or modified in between. Additionally, `statSync` can throw an `EACCES` exception if there are permission restrictions on the target path. Since `gitCommonDir` is called during the fallback git repository check in `resolveAllowedBodyFilePath`, any unhandled exception here will propagate up and trigger a generic `FILE_UNREADABLE` or `FILE_NOT_FOUND` error for the body file itself, leading to misleading error logs. Wrapping the directory check in a `try-catch` block to safely fall back to `dirname(path)` ensures maximum robustness and prevents unexpected failures.

```suggestion
  if (!path) return "";
  let gitDir = dirname(path);
  try {
    if (existsSync(path) && statSync(path).isDirectory()) {
      gitDir = path;
    }
  } catch {
    // Fallback to dirname(path) if statSync fails due to permissions or TOCTOU race conditions
  }
  const topLevel = gitValue(["-C", gitDir, "rev-parse", "--show-toplevel"]);
```

